  "response": "I’m using the repository’s crimes risk workflow to ground the refactor proposal in the exact repeated JSX, then I’ll keep the recommendation scoped to the four invoice forms.\n\nThe flagged subtree is the footer action row—not the invoice fields: the same right-aligned wrapper, Cancel link, and submit button appears in all four files. I’m checking the fixture’s app boundaries before choosing whether “shared” should mean one cross-example module or one local module per runnable example.\n\nFinding `crime_00064` identifies the repeated invoice-form footer:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link href=\"/dashboard/invoices\">Cancel</Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">…</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nExtract it as `InvoiceFormActions`:\n\n```tsx\ntype InvoiceFormActionsProps = {\n  cancelHref?: string;       // defaults to \"/dashboard/invoices\"\n  cancelLabel?: ReactNode;   // defaults to \"Cancel\"\n  children: ReactNode;       // primary-action slot\n};\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Edit Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\nThe component owns the wrapper layout and cancel-link styling. The `children` slot preserves flexibility for submit buttons with pending states, icons, or alternate behavior without expanding the component’s API.\n\nFiles to change:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- New shared component: `dashboard/shared/ui/invoices/invoice-form-actions.tsx`\n\nBecause `final-example` and `starter-example` are separate Next.js applications, placing one component above both app roots may require workspace/import configuration. If those examples must remai